# =============================================================================
# DIYAR — environment
#
# Copy to `.env.local` for development. Nothing here is needed to run `pnpm dev`:
# with no DATABASE_URL the app opens an embedded Postgres (PGlite) under
# apps/web/.data, and the session secrets fall back to a fixed development
# string.
#
# In PRODUCTION every variable below is required. The process refuses to start
# without them — see apps/web/src/instrumentation.ts. That refusal is
# deliberate: a signing key with a default is not a key, and an embedded
# database on a container's disk is not a database.
# =============================================================================

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Database
#
# A Postgres connection string. Behind Supabase's TRANSACTION pooler (port 6543)
# rather than the direct connection: the app opens a pool per instance and a
# direct connection limit is reached long before the traffic justifies it.
#
# The driver is selected by the PRESENCE of this variable, not by NODE_ENV, so a
# staging build gets the real driver without pretending to be production.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres.PROJECT:PASSWORD@aws-0-REGION.pooler.supabase.com:6543/postgres

# How many connections this instance may open. Keep the total across all
# instances comfortably under the database's own limit.
DATABASE_POOL_MAX=10

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Session signing
#
# Two separate keys, because a seller session and an operator session are
# different authorities and one leaked key must not become both. Generate with:
#
#   node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('base64url'))"
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
SELLER_SESSION_SECRET=
OPS_SESSION_SECRET=

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Not yet used — listed so the shape is known before the day it is needed
#
# The SMS sender and the payment gateway are STUBS today, and
# `assertProductionSafe` refuses to boot production while either is configured.
# Setting these does nothing until the real adapters exist; they are here so the
# deployment checklist is complete rather than discovered.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SMS_PROVIDER_KEY=
# PAYMOB_API_KEY=
# BOSTA_API_KEY=
